quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  39,68,"The Trumpet will be blown. And whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will fall senseless, except whomever Allah pleases. Then it will be blown a second time, and they will stand up at once, awaiting."
  39,69,"And the earth will shine with the Light of its Lord, and the Record (of people’s deeds) shall be laid down. And the prophets and the witnesses will be brought forward, and the judgement will be passed between them with justice. And they will not be wronged."
  39,70,"And every soul will be paid in full for what it has done, and He knows best what they do."
  39,71,"And those who disbelieve will be driven to Hell in groups. When they arrive there, its gates will be opened (then). Its keepers will say to them: ‘Did messengers not come to you from among yourselves, reciting upon you the verses of your Lord and warning you about the meeting of this Day of yours.’ They will say: ‘Yes, (they came).’ But the decree of the punishment had become due against the disbelievers."
  39,72,"It will be said: ‘Enter the gates of Hell, to remain there forever. So evil is the (final) abode of the arrogant!’"
  39,73,"Those who were conscious of their Lord will be led to Paradise in (respectful) congregations. When they arrive there, its gates will already be opened. Its keepers will say to them: ‘Peace be upon you! You are welcome! Enter it to remain here forever.’"
  39,74,"They will say: ‘All praise belongs to Allah, Who has fulfilled His promise to us and made us inherit the (everlasting) land, that we may settle in Paradise wherever we wish.’ So, how excellent is the reward for the (righteous) workers!"
